3. inquiry_intent - grain: 1 row per intent. Columns: inquiry_id (FK), intent_id, intent_label, updated_on
4. inquiry_key_point - grain: 1 row per key point. Columns: inquiry_id (FK), key_point_seq, key_point_text, updated_on
5. inquiry_topic  - grain: 1 row per topic. Columns: inquiry_id (FK), topic_seq, topic_text, updated_on

TIMESTAMP REQUIREMENT: In the FINAL tables (asdt_ prefix) only, all timestamp columns (generated_at, updated_on, and any other date/time column) must be declared as TIMESTAMP_NTZ, and all values inserted into them must be explicitly cast with ::TIMESTAMP_NTZ (or TRY_TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ where parsing from string/VARIANT). Work tables (asdw_ prefix) can retain the raw parsed type if it differs, but the final INSERT into the FINAL table must cast to TIMESTAMP_NTZ.

