GENERATE THESE 4 FILES:

File 1: asd_wrapup_summary_load_raw_table.sql
- Loads the raw JSON payload from Blob storage into the raw table's VARIANT column via COPY INTO, following the same pattern as our other shared_snowSQL-based raw loads.

File 2: asd_wrapup_summary_truncate_work_tables.sql
- TRUNCATE TABLE statements for the 5 work tables listed above, in child-to-parent order (intents/key_points/topics first, then inquiry, then conversation) to avoid orphaned-looking state mid-run.

File 3: asd_wrapup_summary_populate_work_tables.sql
- INSERT INTO each of the 5 work tables, SELECTing from the raw table's json_body VARIANT column.
- Use LATERAL FLATTEN to unnest summary:inquiries, then a nested LATERAL FLATTEN on each of intents, key_points, topics_covered within that same inquiry row.
- Generate inquiry_id deterministically, e.g. HASH(conversation_id, inquiry_value.index) or MD5(conversation_id || '-' || inquiry_value.index::string), and reuse that same expression when populating inquiry_intent, inquiry_key_point, inquiry_topic so the FK lines up.
- Do NOT select member_id, member_suffix, or member_name into the inquiry work table.
- Cast all fields out of VARIANT explicitly (::STRING, ::NUMBER, etc.); do not leave typed columns as VARIANT.
- Use TRY_TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ for generated_at/enqueued_time_utc; note we use TRY_TO_DATE (not TRY_TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ) for date-only columns elsewhere, but these are timestamps so TRY_TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ is correct here.
- Populate updated_on as CURRENT_TIMESTAMP()::TIMESTAMP_NTZ on every row.

File 4: asd_wrapup_summary_load_final_tables.sql
- For each of the 5 tables, trim trailing spaces on all string columns in the work table first (UPDATE work table SET col = RTRIM(col)).
- Then INSERT INTO the final table SELECT * FROM the work table, explicitly casting any timestamp column to ::TIMESTAMP_NTZ, using an anti-join (LEFT JOIN final ON PK columns AND UPDATED_ON WHERE final.PK IS NULL) so that rows whose PK + UPDATED_ON combination already exists in the final table are skipped.
- Do this in parent-to-child order (conversation, then inquiry, then intent/key_point/topic) since child FINAL tables reference inquiry_id from the parent.
- PK for the anti-join purposes: conversation -> conversation_id; inquiry -> inquiry_id; inquiry_intent -> (inquiry_id, intent_id); inquiry_key_point -> (inquiry_id, key_point_seq); inquiry_topic -> (inquiry_id, topic_seq).

